# SMIT UI/UX Designer Portfolio – Project Overview

## Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router)
- **UI**: React 19, TypeScript 5.7
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4, PostCSS
- **Components**: Radix UI primitives, Lucide icons, shadcn-style (CVA, clsx, tailwind-merge)

## Path aliases (tsconfig)
- `@/*` → project root (e.g. `@/src/components/portfolio-page`, `@/app/page`)
- `@/assets/*` → `./src/assets/*` (images, Figma assets)

Use these for imports; avoid deep relative paths when a simple `@/...` works.

## Structure
- `app/` – Next routes (`layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`), **single** `globals.css` (theme and Tailwind)
- `src/components/portfolio-page/` – home page: `index.tsx` (PortfolioPage) plus section components (`hero-section.tsx`, `intro-section.tsx`, `services-section.tsx`, `latest-work-section.tsx`, `contact-section.tsx`)
- `lib/imports/` – Figma-derived SVG path data and assets (`svg-u2dm5opmgk.ts`, `svg-uhqxr.tsx`) used by portfolio sections.
- `src/lib/` – shared helpers (e.g. `img-src.ts`)
- Entry: `app/page.tsx` renders `PortfolioPage` from `@/src/components/portfolio-page`

## Conventions
- Prefer functional components and hooks.
- Use Tailwind for layout and styling; inline `style` only when needed (e.g. dynamic values, Figma parity).
- Keep shared utilities and helpers in a dedicated folder (e.g. `src/lib/`) when they grow.
